cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "TriZOD — Re-referenced BMRB chemical-shift dataset for protein disorder"
message: >-
  If you use the TriZOD dataset, please cite it as below, with the version DOI
  of the record you downloaded. The dataset is licensed CC BY 4.0 (see
  LICENSE.md in the deposit); the code that builds it is MIT
  (https://github.com/MarkusHaak/trizod). The data derive from BMRB entries
  (https://bmrb.io); please also acknowledge the BMRB.
type: dataset
abstract: >-
  Per-residue protein-disorder labels (the continuous TriZOD G-score) from
  re-referenced BMRB NMR backbone chemical shifts, one Parquet row per scored
  protein chain, in four nested stringency tiers, with the held-out test set
  TriZOD-test v1.0 and CheZOD117. Training sets are separated from the test
  sets at 30 % identity over 80 % of either chain, searched in both
  directions.
